# Build context for the API image specifically. BuildKit prefers
# `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` over the context root's `.dockerignore`, and this
# file replaces it outright rather than adding to it — so everything the root
# one excludes has to be repeated here.
#
# The entry that matters is `apps/web`. The deps stage installs for three
# workspace projects (root, shared, api), and letting the web app into the
# context makes pnpm see a fourth. It then reads node_modules as stale, tries to
# purge it, and aborts because a Docker build has no TTY to confirm with:
#
#   [ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY]
#
# Nothing in the API depends on the web app, so keeping it out is both the fix
# and the smaller build context.
apps/web

# Never ship the host's install: it is large, platform-specific, and the image
# builds its own.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output, regenerated inside the image.
dist
**/dist
**/.next
**/.open-next
**/.wrangler
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets must not enter the build context. The image takes configuration from
# the environment at runtime.
.env
.env.*

.git
.github
.gitignore
coverage
**/coverage
*.log
.claude
.cursor
.windsurf
.opencode
.clinerules
README.md
DEPLOYMENT.md
AGENTS.md
render.yaml
docker-compose.yml
